WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.680
A farm organizes strategy agents under a shared workspace structure.

2
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.420
Review the agents associated with it before changing settings.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:16.480
The public demo illustrates coordination; it is not evidence that your edition includes every displayed feature.

4
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.860
Use the controls available in your own installed release.

5
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.420
Different strategies can enter the same market or closely related markets.

6
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.260
Grouping agents does not automatically create diversification.

7
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.680
Review total account exposure as well as each agent budget.

8
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.600
Confirm shared limits and do not assume separate cards represent separate pools of trading funds.

9
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.680
Configure limits deliberately and document their intended behavior.

10
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.080
An account drawdown limit differs from a single position stop.

11
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.360
Limits can reject entries while existing positions remain open.

12
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:05.720
Validate the actual behavior in testnet and inspect the venue rather than assuming a toggle eliminated exposure.

13
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:14.440
Where your edition includes Goals, use them to organize targets and review progress.

14
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.900
Read whether the goal is descriptive or connected to an actual control.

15
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.180
A profit target does not make a strategy find safe trades.

16
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.560
Avoid increasing position size simply to catch up with a target.

17
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.140
Before pausing, read the confirmation and understand its scope.

18
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.120
Stopping new entries can leave open orders or positions that still need management.

19
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.720
Closing exposure is a separate consequential action.

20
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.140
Confirm the venue state after any maintenance step and retain a record of what you changed.

21
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:59.040
Your checkpoint is to identify the farm membership, shared exposure, each allocation and the effect of your controls.

22
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.080
Keep a record of the settings before changing them.

23
00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.880
Start with a test configuration you can explain, rather than many agents with overlapping risks.
